# Report format ↔ sample reports (always sync)

When adjusting **either** report product UI or content rules, **always update both sample fixtures in the same change**:

| Product | Live UI | Sample source | Preview URL |
|---------|---------|---------------|-------------|
| Job Fit Snapshot | `components/LiteReportDashboard.tsx` (+ lite prompts/normalize) | `lib/sample-reports.ts` → `getSampleSnapshotReport()` | `/samples?type=job_fit_snapshot` |
| Interview Strategy Guide | `components/FullReportDashboard.tsx` (+ full prompts/normalize) | `lib/sample-reports.ts` → `getSampleStrategyGuideReport()` | `/samples?type=interview_strategy_guide` |

## Checklist (do not skip)

1. Change report layout, copy rules, fields shown/hidden, or Score Summary / Range Evaluation / Beagle Scale behavior.
2. Update **both** sample payloads in `lib/sample-reports.ts` so `/samples` still looks like production.
3. If Strategy Guide embeds Snapshot, ensure Guide sample’s Snapshot layer matches the Snapshot sample rules.
4. Run/adjust `__tests__/unit/sample-reports.test.ts` if structure changes.
5. Commit samples with the UI/prompt change — never leave samples stale for “later”.

## Current Snapshot content rules (as of 2026-07-18)

- **Layout**: one-page slide frame (`LiteReportDashboard`) with three numbered sections — 1 role core, 2 market pay band, 3 fit score / missing keywords / apply call. Upgrade locks sit inside sections 2 and 3. No upgrade CTA under the slide.
- JobBeagle evaluates fit — it is **not** a resume coach. Line-by-line rewrites appear only on Interview Guide item 3.
- Strategy Guide uses **top horizontal nav** for the seven items: Role core · Market pay · Fit · Pay landing · Company · Questions · Negotiation. It opens on item 1. Source links live inside items 4–6.
- All report surfaces (Snapshot, Guide, `/samples`, `/report`) center as a column; **sample pages** place an independent Sample notice card on the **left**, top-aligned with the report frame (`sm:items-start`).
- Sample notice **SAMPLE** uses `SampleMark variant="notice"` (narrow-card sizing). Report frames use default `variant="report"`. Do not override size/tracking via className — Tailwind utility conflicts will clip to “SAMP”.
- Frame borders use bright blue (`border-blue-500`). Shell width: `REPORT_SHELL_WIDTH` = `max-w-[98vw]` — **never rem-cap** (e.g. 100rem≈1600px creates a centered island on large monitors).
- Samples + `/report` wrap content in `ReportFitStage` (CSS `zoom` up to 1.5 from a 1280px baseline) so the slide scales up on large displays.
- Tailwind `content` must include `./constants/**` so shell width utilities in `report-frame.ts` are generated.

